            <ArticleTitle>Pseudodissection of the coronary artery: a variation caused by interventional tools.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>298-300</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During PTCA immediate decisions often must be made on the basis of a less than optimum data set. We present a combination of factors which produce an incorrect perception of a coronary artery dissection. This potential must be understood by the interventionalist to avoid misdiagnosis and inappropriate therapeutic maneuvers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
